/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
177 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 100 0 R
/E (The first discussion focused on whether the project is delivering what was originally envisaged. Overall, the work was considered to be on track, while participants highlighted the need to strengthen the links between activities and deliverables across Work Packages.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
178 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 100 0 R
/E (The discussion also focused on who should benefit from the project's results, identifying NSIs, students and the project community itself as key target groups. Participants stressed the importance of producing citable publications, to contribute to the growing knowledge base on AI. The creation of training and example datasets for different tasks was also identified as a valuable way to make the project's results more practical and reusable.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
179 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 100 0 R
/T (From Theory to Practice: Standards, Methodology and Implementation)
/E (From Theory to Practice: Standards, Methodology and Implementation)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
180 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 100 0 R
/E (The second question explored how standards and methodological work connect with the use cases developed across the project. Participants discussed the effectiveness of the TMLE model and, more broadly, the challenge of translating theoretical principles into real-world applications. Two areas emerged as particularly important for further work: reproducibility and the measurement of AI maturity. Addressing these challenges will require a collaborative approach, bringing together technical experts and combining knowledge from data science, statistical analysis and regulatory frameworks. This multidisciplinary perspective will be essential to ensure that methodological developments can be effectively implemented in official statistics.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [7 294 0 R 9]
>>
endobj
