191 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 101 0 R
/E (Looking beyond the project's lifetime, participants discussed how its achievements can be maintained, shared and further developed. A key question was who will take ownership of the project's repositories and technical assets once the project ends.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
192 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 101 0 R
/T (The project's achievements were seen as stepping stones for future developments, but their long-term use may depend on infrastructure and technologies such as Onyxia. Establishing a community group to support continuity was therefore proposed as one possible way to maintain collaboration and knowledge sharing. Regional conferences were also suggested as a means of reaching domain specialists and new communities and broadening the project's impact.)
/E (The project's achievements were seen as stepping stones for future developments, but their long-term use may depend on infrastructure and technologies such as Onyxia. Establishing a community group to support continuity was therefore proposed as one possible way to maintain collaboration and knowledge sharing. Regional conferences were also suggested as a means of reaching domain specialists and new communities and broadening the project's impact.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
193 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 101 0 R
/T (What Comes Next? A Vision Beyond Three Years)
/E (What Comes Next? A Vision Beyond Three Years)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
194 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 101 0 R
/T (The final discussion looked further ahead, asking what could be developed once the current project comes to an end. Several emerging areas were identified as potential priorities, including agentic AI, LLMs in production, digital sovereignty and data dissemination.)
/E (The final discussion looked further ahead, asking what could be developed once the current project comes to an end. Several emerging areas were identified as potential priorities, including agentic AI, LLMs in production, digital sovereignty and data dissemination.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
195 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 101 0 R
/T (Future work could also build on a stronger co-development approach, involving not only other NSIs but potentially central banks and organisations such as the JRC. Participants discussed the possibility of benchmarking models, countries and datasets according to the specific needs of NSIs, as well as testing the project's approaches with new NSIs.)
/E (Future work could also build on a stronger co-development approach, involving not only other NSIs but potentially central banks and organisations such as the JRC. Participants discussed the possibility of benchmarking models, countries and datasets according to the specific needs of NSIs, as well as testing the project's approaches with new NSIs.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
