805 0 obj
<<
/Title (The main objectives of AIML4OS are to explore the use)
/Dest [10 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 305 0 R
/Prev 693 0 R
/Next 869 0 R
>>
endobj
806 0 obj
<<
/Title (LOOKING AHEAD: REFLECTING ON THREE YEARS OF COLLABORATION AND SHAPING THE FUTURE)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 305 0 R
/Prev 870 0 R
/Next 694 0 R
>>
endobj
807 0 obj
<<
/Title (The project's achievements were seen as stepping stones for future developments, but their long-term use may depend on infrastructure and technologies such as Onyxia. Establishing a community group to support continuity was therefore proposed as one possible way to maintain collaboration and knowledge sharing. Regional conferences were also suggested as a means of reaching domain specialists and new communities and broadening the project's impact.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 695 0 R
>>
endobj
808 0 obj
<<
/Title (The final discussion looked further ahead, asking what could be developed once the current project comes to an end. Several emerging areas were identified as potential priorities, including agentic AI, LLMs in production, digital sovereignty and data dissemination.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 696 0 R
/Next 809 0 R
>>
endobj
809 0 obj
<<
/Title (Future work could also build on a stronger co-development approach, involving not only other NSIs but potentially central banks and organisations such as the JRC. Participants discussed the possibility of benchmarking models, countries and datasets according to the specific needs of NSIs, as well as testing the project's approaches with new NSIs.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 696 0 R
/Prev 808 0 R
>>
endobj
810 0 obj
<<
/Title (THE FIRST EUROPEAN AIML4OS FUNATHON)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 697 0 R
/Next 811 0 R
>>
endobj
811 0 obj
<<
/Title (Building AI Skills Across the European Statistical System)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 697 0 R
/Prev 810 0 R
/First 871 0 R
/Last 871 0 R
/Count -1
>>
endobj
812 0 obj
<<
/Title (Participant Feedback)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 698 0 R
>>
endobj
813 0 obj
<<
/Title (Exploring agentic web scraping, AI-supported metadata management and statistical reporting assessment)
/Dest [15 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 555 0 R
/Prev 699 0 R
/Next 700 0 R
>>
endobj
814 0 obj
<<
/Title (Another important theme was digital sovereignty and practical implementation in environments that are realistic for national statistical institutes. The work therefore focused on approaches that could reasonably be run in an)
/Dest [15 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 700 0 R
/Next 872 0 R
>>
endobj
815 0 obj
<<
/Title (The sprint also contributed material for upcoming deliverables, including reflections on architecture, evaluation, documentation and practical implementation. The results will be further documented in the repository and used as input to the continued AIML4OS work on the responsible and practical use of generative AI in official statistics.)
/Dest [15 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 700 0 R
/Prev 872 0 R
>>
endobj
816 0 obj
<<
/Title (Feedback under the heading explainability covered conceptual clarification, the importance of individual words in text data, variable importance, trust and reliability.)
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 557 0 R
/Prev 702 0 R
/Next 817 0 R
>>
endobj
817 0 obj
<<
/Title (Feedback on reproducibility included, among other things, consideration of the production pipeline and the skills required. Reproducing an entire pipeline is more complex than reproducing individual steps, particularly within NSIs.)
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 557 0 R
/Prev 816 0 R
/Next 703 0 R
>>
endobj
818 0 obj
<<
/Title (WPS ROADMAP)
/Dest [17 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 307 0 R
/Prev 704 0 R
/Next 819 0 R
>>
endobj
819 0 obj
<<
/Title (USE)
/Dest [17 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 307 0 R
/Prev 818 0 R
/Next 705 0 R
>>
